('78e95338-416b-59b3-a434-bd4c80f86589','956218a0-3221-5fbe-9a62-7fed9012cc40',6,null,null,'spoken & written','if something is divided or shared among a group of people, each person is given a part of it',null,null,'اگر چیزی بین گروهی از مردم تقسیم یا تقسیم شود، به هر فرد بخشی از آن داده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"A father’s property was divided among his heirs.","translation":"دارایی پدری بین ورثه او تقسیم شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001841939.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('a31e09eb-1533-5aac-9beb-97da62c2bdbe','956218a0-3221-5fbe-9a62-7fed9012cc40',7,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'among yourselves/ourselves/themselves','در میان، بین (گروهی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('dabe40ae-eb12-55e0-8767-c87ef1f02f9f','9bc6fc88-a001-5480-b888-de7fb61f2184',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a strong feeling of wanting to hurt or criticize someone because they have done something bad to you or been unkind to you',null,null,'خشم، عصبانیت، غضب','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['be filled with anger/be full of anger His face was suddenly filled with anger.','be shaking with anger My aunt was shaking with anger as she left the room.','be seething with anger (= be extremely angry ) Seething with anger and frustration, Polly pushed back her chair and stood up.','express your anger ( also vent your anger formal ) (= show your anger ) Demonstrators expressed their anger by burning American flags.','hide your anger For a second he was unable to hide his anger.','control/contain your anger I could not control my anger any longer.','arouse/provoke anger ( also stir up anger informal ) (= make people angry ) The referee’s decision provoked anger among the fans.','fuel anger (= make people even more angry ) The row could fuel growing anger among the Labour party.','somebody’s anger goes away/subsides/fades (= it stops ) I counted to ten and waited for my anger to go away. His anger slowly subsided.','deep/great/fierce anger There is deep anger against the occupying forces.','growing/rising/mounting anger There is growing anger among drivers over the rise in fuel prices.','widespread anger (= among many people ) The decision to build the airport has provoked widespread anger.','public/popular anger By now public anger in America was mounting.','suppressed/pent-up anger (= that you have tried not to show ) Her voice shook with suppressed anger.','real anger There is real anger about the amount of money that has been wasted.','righteous anger often disapproving (= anger felt when you think something should not be allowed to happen ) The speech was full of righteous anger against the West.','a fit/outburst of anger (= an occasion when someone suddenly becomes angry ) His occasional outbursts of anger shocked those around him.','a feeling of anger He was overcome by a sudden feeling of anger against the people who had put him there.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"There is growing anger among the people against the government.","translation":"خشم مردم علیه حکومت رو به افزایش است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001738686.mp3"},{"sentence":"She struggled to control her anger at her son’s disobedience.","translation":"او تلاش کرد تا خشم خود را از نافرمانی پسرش کنترل کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001738685.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘That’s a lie!’ he shouted in anger.","translation":"او با عصبانیت فریاد زد: \"این یک دروغ است!\"","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000069.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('9c8ae139-889a-5ba0-977e-c74192985553','9bc6fc88-a001-5480-b888-de7fb61f2184',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'do/use something in anger','خشم، عصبانیت، غضب','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['be filled with anger/be full of anger His face was suddenly filled with anger.','be shaking with anger My aunt was shaking with anger as she left the room.','be seething with anger (= be extremely angry ) Seething with anger and frustration, Polly pushed back her chair and stood up.','express your anger ( also vent your anger formal ) (= show your anger ) Demonstrators expressed their anger by burning American flags.','hide your anger For a second he was unable to hide his anger.','control/contain your anger I could not control my anger any longer.','arouse/provoke anger ( also stir up anger informal ) (= make people angry ) The referee’s decision provoked anger among the fans.','fuel anger (= make people even more angry ) The row could fuel growing anger among the Labour party.','somebody’s anger goes away/subsides/fades (= it stops ) I counted to ten and waited for my anger to go away. His anger slowly subsided.','deep/great/fierce anger There is deep anger against the occupying forces.','growing/rising/mounting anger There is growing anger among drivers over the rise in fuel prices.','widespread anger (= among many people ) The decision to build the airport has provoked widespread anger.','public/popular anger By now public anger in America was mounting.','suppressed/pent-up anger (= that you have tried not to show ) Her voice shook with suppressed anger.','real anger There is real anger about the amount of money that has been wasted.','righteous anger often disapproving (= anger felt when you think something should not be allowed to happen ) The speech was full of righteous anger against the West.','a fit/outburst of anger (= an occasion when someone suddenly becomes angry ) His occasional outbursts of anger shocked those around him.','a feeling of anger He was overcome by a sudden feeling of anger against the people who had put him there.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('c0ed15de-6099-576e-b9cc-54e290cdaf5e','23444bd6-fb07-5d12-9131-c6603d955530',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to make someone angry',null,null,'کسی را عصبانی کردن',array['annoy']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"What angered me most was his total lack of remorse.","translation":"چیزی که من را بیشتر عصبانی کرد عدم پشیمانی کامل او بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000940328.mp3"},{"sentence":"Environmental groups were disappointed and angered by the president’s decision.","translation":"گروه های محیط زیست از تصمیم رئیس جمهور ناامید و خشمگین شدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001738696.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('95740f5f-6464-557a-85b7-7d78abf7a411','8861a635-37f0-502d-aeae-fda4cb571ccf',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the space between two straight lines or surfaces that join each other, measured in degrees',null,'right angle','زاویه؛ زاویه دید، منظر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"an angle of 45°","translation":"زاویه 45 درجه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000940353.mp3"},{"sentence":"the angles of a triangle","translation":"زوایای یک مثلث","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001738701.mp3"},{"sentence":"You didn’t measure the angle accurately.","translation":"شما زاویه را دقیق اندازه نگرفتید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001738702.mp3"},{"sentence":"the angle between walls and ceiling","translation":"زاویه بین دیوارها و سقف","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001738705.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('5d1fba91-d3fb-58db-b4c8-02690d18ac34','8861a635-37f0-502d-aeae-fda4cb571ccf',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a way of considering a problem or situation',null,null,'راهی برای در نظر گرفتن یک مشکل یا موقعیت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We’re approaching the issue from many different angles .","translation":"ما از زوایای مختلف به موضوع نگاه می کنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001738706.mp3"},{"sentence":"Look at every angle of the situation.","translation":"به هر زاویه ای از موقعیت نگاه کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001738712.mp3"},{"sentence":"There’s another angle to this question.","translation":"این سوال زاویه دیگری هم دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001738718.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('185b3439-3de6-5513-b5ab-47cea9d066e8','8861a635-37f0-502d-aeae-fda4cb571ccf',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a position from which you look at something or photograph it',null,null,'موقعیتی که از آن به چیزی نگاه می کنید یا از آن عکس می گیرید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"This drawing of the monastery was done from an unusual angle.","translation":"این ترسیم صومعه از زاویه ای غیرعادی انجام شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000940361.mp3"},{"sentence":"Some of the pictures have strange camera angles.","translation":"برخی از تصاویر زوایای دوربین عجیبی دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001738724.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('d8acd3f0-7d53-5fb7-a108-ed7ea4a071c0','8861a635-37f0-502d-aeae-fda4cb571ccf',4,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'at an angle','زاویه؛ زاویه دید، منظر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('0586bd96-d0ab-5a8a-8519-a5edeb4749e0','8861a635-37f0-502d-aeae-fda4cb571ccf',5,null,null,'spoken & written','the shape formed when two lines or surfaces join',null,null,'شکلی که هنگام اتصال دو خط یا سطح ایجاد می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"My head struck the angle of the shelf.","translation":"سرم به زاویه قفسه برخورد کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000940374.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('365b6f44-18b2-593f-9151-4c387c007b6c','835de03b-5b68-5130-99f1-0578150097c0',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to move or place something so that it is not straight or upright',null,null,'حرکت دادن یا قرار دادن چیزی به گونه ای که مستقیم یا قائم نباشد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a mirror angled to reflect light from a window","translation":"یک آینه زاویه دار برای بازتاب نور از پنجره","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000940384.mp3"},{"sentence":"Philip angled his chair towards the door.","translation":"فیلیپ صندلی خود را به سمت در زاویه داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001738730.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('22ecc1d1-27c1-5745-a19e-1a42a70061c0','835de03b-5b68-5130-99f1-0578150097c0',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to present information from a particular point of view or for a specific group of people',null,null,'برای ارائه اطلاعات از یک دیدگاه خاص یا برای گروه خاصی از مردم','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The book is angled towards a business audience.","translation":"زاویه این کتاب به سمت مخاطبان تجاری است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000940389.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('e5325dd0-eaa8-500c-a975-18809a31feb1','666df352-1911-55dd-8369-2e72e2947def',1,null,null,'spoken & written','feeling strong emotions which make you want to shout at someone or hurt them because they have behaved in an unfair , cruel , offensive etc way, or because you think that a situation is unfair, unacceptable etc',null,null,'خشمگین، عصبانی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I was angry because he hadn’t told me his plans.","translation":"عصبانی بودم چون برنامه هایش را به من نگفته بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001656855.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was beginning to get angry .","translation":"کم کم داشت عصبانی می شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001656847.mp3"},{"sentence":"His comments brought an angry response from opposition politicians.","translation":"اظهارات او با واکنش خشم آلود سیاستمداران مخالف مواجه شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000981080.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘Calm down, ’ she said, looking at his angry face.","translation":"او در حالی که به چهره عصبانی او نگاه می کرد گفت: آرام باش.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-002091686.mp3"},{"sentence":"Jesse laughed, which made me even angrier .","translation":"جسی خندید که عصبانی ترم کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000981089.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘Please don’t be angry with me, ’ she said.","translation":"او گفت: لطفا از دست من عصبانی نباش.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001656851.mp3"},{"sentence":"They are angry at the way they have been treated.","translation":"آنها از نحوه برخورد با آنها عصبانی هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce6exa_00050.mp3"},{"sentence":"Kate’s still so angry about the whole thing.","translation":"کیت هنوز از همه چیز خیلی عصبانی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000981086.mp3"},{"sentence":"The workers are angry that they haven’t been paid for the week.","translation":"کارگران از اینکه یک هفته حقوق نگرفته اند عصبانی هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001656863.mp3"}]'::jsonb,9),
