('d131f849-1a92-524f-9392-6ca6f338ac84','ad48b6eb-36b4-5456-9eb3-a9c07c6b8016',1,null,null,'spoken & written','relating to the people who live in a country','[ only before noun ]','civil liberty , civil rights','مدنی، غیرنظامی؛ وقار‌مند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['civil war (= fighting between groups of people in the same country ) His family fled Spain during the Spanish civil war.','civil rights (= the right to vote, be treated fairly etc that everyone should have ) Black people marched in defence of their civil rights.','civil liberties/liberty (= the right to be free to do what you want within the law ) Detention without trial threatens our civil liberties.','civil disobedience/unrest (= when people protest or behave violently ) Unemployment has provoked widespread civil unrest.','civil disturbances/strife (= civil unrest ) Troops have been called in to deal with civil disturbances.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('9cc9c3cd-4933-5fcc-9496-faebfa398b98','ad48b6eb-36b4-5456-9eb3-a9c07c6b8016',2,null,null,'spoken & written','relating to the ordinary people or things in a country that are not part of military , government, or religious organizations','[ only before noun ]',null,'مربوط به مردم عادی یا چیزهایی در یک کشور که بخشی از سازمان های نظامی، دولتی یا مذهبی نیستند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['civil war (= fighting between groups of people in the same country ) His family fled Spain during the Spanish civil war.','civil rights (= the right to vote, be treated fairly etc that everyone should have ) Black people marched in defence of their civil rights.','civil liberties/liberty (= the right to be free to do what you want within the law ) Detention without trial threatens our civil liberties.','civil disobedience/unrest (= when people protest or behave violently ) Unemployment has provoked widespread civil unrest.','civil disturbances/strife (= civil unrest ) Troops have been called in to deal with civil disturbances.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"They were married in a civil ceremony in May.","translation":"آنها در ماه مه در یک مراسم مدنی ازدواج کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001694112.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('044bcdd5-4914-508b-8b49-763d1ada6d5b','ad48b6eb-36b4-5456-9eb3-a9c07c6b8016',3,null,null,'spoken & written','relating to the laws about the private affairs of citizens , such as laws about business or property , rather than laws about crime','[ only before noun ]',null,'مربوط به قوانین مربوط به امور خصوصی شهروندان، مانند قوانین مربوط به تجارت یا دارایی، به جای قوانین مربوط به جرم و جنایت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['civil war (= fighting between groups of people in the same country ) His family fled Spain during the Spanish civil war.','civil rights (= the right to vote, be treated fairly etc that everyone should have ) Black people marched in defence of their civil rights.','civil liberties/liberty (= the right to be free to do what you want within the law ) Detention without trial threatens our civil liberties.','civil disobedience/unrest (= when people protest or behave violently ) Unemployment has provoked widespread civil unrest.','civil disturbances/strife (= civil unrest ) Troops have been called in to deal with civil disturbances.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Many civil cases can be settled out of court.","translation":"بسیاری از پرونده های مدنی را می توان خارج از دادگاه حل و فصل کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000887063.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('5c19edff-1cd7-53dc-a2f7-2f06eaadb8a9','ad48b6eb-36b4-5456-9eb3-a9c07c6b8016',4,null,null,'spoken & written','polite in a formal but not very friendly way',null,null,'مودب به روشی رسمی اما نه خیلی دوستانه','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['civil war (= fighting between groups of people in the same country ) His family fled Spain during the Spanish civil war.','civil rights (= the right to vote, be treated fairly etc that everyone should have ) Black people marched in defence of their civil rights.','civil liberties/liberty (= the right to be free to do what you want within the law ) Detention without trial threatens our civil liberties.','civil disobedience/unrest (= when people protest or behave violently ) Unemployment has provoked widespread civil unrest.','civil disturbances/strife (= civil unrest ) Troops have been called in to deal with civil disturbances.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Try at least to be civil.","translation":"سعی کنید حداقل مدنی باشید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000887077.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('ad677a60-7180-5225-a645-f8fe62c6b73d','203ff6d3-0931-5b23-83ef-7b1c3c8c7d4e',1,'truth','حقیقت','spoken & written','to state that something is true, even though it has not been proved','[ transitive ]',null,'ادعا کردن، مدعی شدن؛ مطالبه کردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['claim responsibility (= say that you are responsible for something bad ) Following the attack, a man phoned a newspaper claiming responsibility.','claim credit (= say that you are responsible for something good ) Political parties always claim credit for economic growth.','claim victory (= say that you are the winner ) The election results were in and the president was able to claim victory.','claim descent (= say that you are related to someone important who lived a long time ago ) He claimed descent from Beethoven.','wrongly/rightly This hotel can rightly claim that it has some of the best views on the island.','falsely/rightfully (= wrongly/rightly ) Some manufacturers falsely claim that their products are environmentally friendly.','justifiably (= with good reasons ) They can justifiably claim to be the top team in the country.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The product claims that it can make you thin without dieting.","translation":"این محصول ادعا می کند که می تواند شما را بدون رژیم لاغر کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa020033.mp3"},{"sentence":"No responsible therapist will claim to cure your insomnia.","translation":"هیچ درمانگر مسئولی ادعا نمی کند که بی خوابی شما را درمان می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001662836.mp3"},{"sentence":"I don’t claim to be a feminist, but I’d like to see more women in top jobs.","translation":"من ادعا نمی کنم که یک فمینیست هستم، اما دوست دارم زنان بیشتری را در مشاغل برتر ببینم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000887257.mp3"},{"sentence":"The girls claim to have seen the fairies.","translation":"دخترها ادعا می کنند که پری ها را دیده اند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000887260.mp3"},{"sentence":"The group claimed responsibility for the bombings.","translation":"این گروه مسئولیت این انفجارها را بر عهده گرفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001789813.mp3"},{"sentence":"Opposition leaders will claim victory if the turnout is lower than 50%.","translation":"رهبران اپوزیسیون اگر مشارکت کمتر از 50 درصد باشد ادعای پیروزی خواهند کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001662842.mp3"},{"sentence":"A letter appeared in ‘The Times’ claiming Fleming as the discoverer of penicillin.","translation":"نامه ای در \"تایمز\" ظاهر شد که فلمینگ را کاشف پنی سیلین می دانست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001662848.mp3"},{"sentence":"It has been claimed that he was difficult to work with.","translation":"ادعا شده است که کار با او سخت بوده است.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,8),
('ddbce973-af8a-57ee-8536-c5dfd9b27abc','203ff6d3-0931-5b23-83ef-7b1c3c8c7d4e',2,'money','پول','spoken & written','to officially demand or receive money from an organization because you have a right to it','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'به طور رسمی از یک سازمان درخواست یا دریافت پول کنید زیرا حق دارید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['claim responsibility (= say that you are responsible for something bad ) Following the attack, a man phoned a newspaper claiming responsibility.','claim credit (= say that you are responsible for something good ) Political parties always claim credit for economic growth.','claim victory (= say that you are the winner ) The election results were in and the president was able to claim victory.','claim descent (= say that you are related to someone important who lived a long time ago ) He claimed descent from Beethoven.','wrongly/rightly This hotel can rightly claim that it has some of the best views on the island.','falsely/rightfully (= wrongly/rightly ) Some manufacturers falsely claim that their products are environmentally friendly.','justifiably (= with good reasons ) They can justifiably claim to be the top team in the country.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"He should be able to claim the price of the ticket back.","translation":"او باید بتواند قیمت بلیط را پس بگیرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001662852.mp3"},{"sentence":"You can claim on the insurance if you have an accident while on holiday.","translation":"اگر در تعطیلات دچار حادثه شدید می توانید از بیمه نامه مطالبه کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000887270.mp3"},{"sentence":"If you’re still not satisfied, you may be able to claim compensation .","translation":"اگر هنوز راضی نیستید، ممکن است بتوانید مطالبه غرامت کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001662854.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('6683f8de-c331-581c-b3c0-0838cd2c2442','203ff6d3-0931-5b23-83ef-7b1c3c8c7d4e',3,'legal right','حق قانونی','spoken & written','to state that you have a right to take or have something that is legally yours','[ transitive ]',null,'بیان کنید که حق دارید چیزی را بگیرید یا داشته باشید که قانوناً مال شماست','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['claim responsibility (= say that you are responsible for something bad ) Following the attack, a man phoned a newspaper claiming responsibility.','claim credit (= say that you are responsible for something good ) Political parties always claim credit for economic growth.','claim victory (= say that you are the winner ) The election results were in and the president was able to claim victory.','claim descent (= say that you are related to someone important who lived a long time ago ) He claimed descent from Beethoven.','wrongly/rightly This hotel can rightly claim that it has some of the best views on the island.','falsely/rightfully (= wrongly/rightly ) Some manufacturers falsely claim that their products are environmentally friendly.','justifiably (= with good reasons ) They can justifiably claim to be the top team in the country.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The majority of those who claim asylum are genuine refugees.","translation":"اکثریت کسانی که ادعای پناهندگی می کنند، پناهندگان واقعی هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001662859.mp3"},{"sentence":"Lost property can be claimed between 10 a.m. and 4 p.m.","translation":"اموال گمشده بین ساعت 10 صبح تا 4 بعد از ظهر قابل مطالبه است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000887280.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('848ec342-346d-5fa9-8a5f-aa4ce0f529af','203ff6d3-0931-5b23-83ef-7b1c3c8c7d4e',4,'death','مرگ','spoken & written','if a war, accident etc claims lives, people die because of it – used especially in news reports','[ transitive ]',null,'اگر جنگ، تصادف و غیره جان افراد را بگیرد، مردم به خاطر آن می میرند - به ویژه در گزارش های خبری استفاده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['claim responsibility (= say that you are responsible for something bad ) Following the attack, a man phoned a newspaper claiming responsibility.','claim credit (= say that you are responsible for something good ) Political parties always claim credit for economic growth.','claim victory (= say that you are the winner ) The election results were in and the president was able to claim victory.','claim descent (= say that you are related to someone important who lived a long time ago ) He claimed descent from Beethoven.','wrongly/rightly This hotel can rightly claim that it has some of the best views on the island.','falsely/rightfully (= wrongly/rightly ) Some manufacturers falsely claim that their products are environmentally friendly.','justifiably (= with good reasons ) They can justifiably claim to be the top team in the country.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The earthquake has so far claimed over 3,000 lives.","translation":"این زمین لرزه تاکنون جان بیش از 3000 نفر را گرفته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000887285.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('80dfe041-0b2c-51f4-9b27-b5a65b8539af','203ff6d3-0931-5b23-83ef-7b1c3c8c7d4e',5,'attention','توجه','spoken & written','if something claims your attention, you notice and consider it carefully','[ transitive ]',null,'اگر چیزی توجه شما را جلب کند، متوجه می شوید و آن را با دقت بررسی می کنید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['claim responsibility (= say that you are responsible for something bad ) Following the attack, a man phoned a newspaper claiming responsibility.','claim credit (= say that you are responsible for something good ) Political parties always claim credit for economic growth.','claim victory (= say that you are the winner ) The election results were in and the president was able to claim victory.','claim descent (= say that you are related to someone important who lived a long time ago ) He claimed descent from Beethoven.','wrongly/rightly This hotel can rightly claim that it has some of the best views on the island.','falsely/rightfully (= wrongly/rightly ) Some manufacturers falsely claim that their products are environmentally friendly.','justifiably (= with good reasons ) They can justifiably claim to be the top team in the country.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The military conflict continues to claim our undivided attention.","translation":"درگیری نظامی همچنان توجه ما را به خود جلب می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000887290.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('e52f6e96-51f8-5584-907e-c0e31adf33b1','3696b85d-e5a4-5479-81e1-5785a349d2dc',1,'truth','حقیقت','spoken & written','a statement that something is true, even though it has not been proved',null,null,'ادعا، بهانه؛ مطالبه؛ ادعای زمین','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['false His claims were later found to be false.','unfounded/unsubstantiated (= not based on truth or evidence ) These claims of discrimination are completely unfounded.','extravagant claims (= clearly not true ) Some manufacturers make extravagant claims for their products.','competing claims the competing claims of the political parties','conflicting claims (= saying that different things are true ) The reports contained conflicting claims of the number of people killed.','make a claim He made extravagant claims about the benefits of the diet.','deny a claim (= say it is not true ) Government officials denied claims that the country possessed chemical weapons.','dispute/reject a claim (= say it is not true ) The prime minister rejected claims of a disagreement within his party.','support a claim The court found no evidence to support her claim.','back up a claim (= support it ) They challenged him to back up his claims with evidence.','accept a claim Many scientists were reluctant to accept his claims.','challenge a claim (= say that you do not believe it is true ) Washington continued to challenge the claim that global warming is partly caused by carbon dioxide.','investigate a claim Detectives are investigating claims that the two officials took bribes.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Gould rejected claims that he had acted irresponsibly.","translation":"گولد ادعاهایی مبنی بر اینکه غیرمسئولانه عمل کرده است را رد کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001078607.mp3"},{"sentence":"firms that make false claims about their products","translation":"شرکت هایی که ادعاهای نادرستی در مورد محصولات خود دارند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663078.mp3"},{"sentence":"They made claims they couldn’t live up to.","translation":"آنها ادعاهایی کردند که نمی توانستند به آن عمل کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001789814.mp3"},{"sentence":"the competing claims of scientists","translation":"ادعاهای رقیب دانشمندان","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663084.mp3"},{"sentence":"The police denied claims that the men were tortured.","translation":"پلیس ادعای شکنجه این افراد را رد کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663088.mp3"},{"sentence":"Evidence to support these claims is still lacking.","translation":"شواهدی برای حمایت از این ادعاها هنوز وجود ندارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663089.mp3"},{"sentence":"his claim to be the rightful owner of the painting","translation":"ادعای او مبنی بر اینکه مالک واقعی نقاشی است","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001078610.mp3"},{"sentence":"I make no claim to understand the complexities of the situation.","translation":"من هیچ ادعایی برای درک پیچیدگی های شرایط ندارم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001078617.mp3"}]'::jsonb,8),
('6470c10f-758e-5951-9684-93d1e6337ce9','3696b85d-e5a4-5479-81e1-5785a349d2dc',2,'money','پول','spoken & written','an official request for money that you think you have a right to',null,null,'درخواست رسمی پولی که فکر می کنید حق دارید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['false His claims were later found to be false.','unfounded/unsubstantiated (= not based on truth or evidence ) These claims of discrimination are completely unfounded.','extravagant claims (= clearly not true ) Some manufacturers make extravagant claims for their products.','competing claims the competing claims of the political parties','conflicting claims (= saying that different things are true ) The reports contained conflicting claims of the number of people killed.','make a claim He made extravagant claims about the benefits of the diet.','deny a claim (= say it is not true ) Government officials denied claims that the country possessed chemical weapons.','dispute/reject a claim (= say it is not true ) The prime minister rejected claims of a disagreement within his party.','support a claim The court found no evidence to support her claim.','back up a claim (= support it ) They challenged him to back up his claims with evidence.','accept a claim Many scientists were reluctant to accept his claims.','challenge a claim (= say that you do not believe it is true ) Washington continued to challenge the claim that global warming is partly caused by carbon dioxide.','investigate a claim Detectives are investigating claims that the two officials took bribes.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"claims for compensation","translation":"ادعای غرامت","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663101.mp3"},{"sentence":"He lost his claim for unfair dismissal.","translation":"او ادعای اخراج ناعادلانه خود را از دست داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663104.mp3"},{"sentence":"All claims should be made in writing.","translation":"تمام ادعاها باید به صورت کتبی ارائه شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001078589.mp3"},{"sentence":"Fill in and return the claim form as soon as it arrives.","translation":"فرم درخواست را به محض رسیدن پر کرده و برگردانید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663105.mp3"},{"sentence":"The insurance company cannot meet (= pay ) such enormous claims .","translation":"شرکت بیمه نمی تواند چنین مطالبات هنگفتی را برآورده کند (= پرداخت).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001078599.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('ab3fa4b4-1b81-5c68-8274-dfacfa7f3435','3696b85d-e5a4-5479-81e1-5785a349d2dc',3,'rights','حقوق','spoken & written','a right to do something or to have something, especially because it belongs to you or because you deserve it',null,null,'حق انجام کاری یا داشتن چیزی، به خصوص به این دلیل که به شما تعلق دارد یا به این دلیل که لیاقت آن را دارید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['false His claims were later found to be false.','unfounded/unsubstantiated (= not based on truth or evidence ) These claims of discrimination are completely unfounded.','extravagant claims (= clearly not true ) Some manufacturers make extravagant claims for their products.','competing claims the competing claims of the political parties','conflicting claims (= saying that different things are true ) The reports contained conflicting claims of the number of people killed.','make a claim He made extravagant claims about the benefits of the diet.','deny a claim (= say it is not true ) Government officials denied claims that the country possessed chemical weapons.','dispute/reject a claim (= say it is not true ) The prime minister rejected claims of a disagreement within his party.','support a claim The court found no evidence to support her claim.','back up a claim (= support it ) They challenged him to back up his claims with evidence.','accept a claim Many scientists were reluctant to accept his claims.','challenge a claim (= say that you do not believe it is true ) Washington continued to challenge the claim that global warming is partly caused by carbon dioxide.','investigate a claim Detectives are investigating claims that the two officials took bribes.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Surely they have a rightful claim on their father’s land?","translation":"آیا آنها در زمین پدرشان حق دارند؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001078639.mp3"},{"sentence":"The Maldives pressed its claim to hold the summit.","translation":"مالدیو ادعای خود مبنی بر برگزاری این نشست را مطرح کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663119.mp3"},{"sentence":"Philip feared Edward would lay claim to the Scottish crown.","translation":"فیلیپ می ترسید که ادوارد ادعای تاج و تخت اسکاتلند را داشته باشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663125.mp3"},{"sentence":"the competing claims of parents and teachers","translation":"ادعاهای رقیب والدین و معلمان","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663129.mp3"},{"sentence":"A woman who has given a man children will always have a claim on his love.","translation":"زنی که به مردی بچه داده است همیشه ادعای عشق او را دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663135.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('7a771e20-c490-524b-97d6-b4879cf4771d','3696b85d-e5a4-5479-81e1-5785a349d2dc',4,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'stake your claim (for something)','ادعا، بهانه؛ مطالبه؛ ادعای زمین','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['false His claims were later found to be false.','unfounded/unsubstantiated (= not based on truth or evidence ) These claims of discrimination are completely unfounded.','extravagant claims (= clearly not true ) Some manufacturers make extravagant claims for their products.','competing claims the competing claims of the political parties','conflicting claims (= saying that different things are true ) The reports contained conflicting claims of the number of people killed.','make a claim He made extravagant claims about the benefits of the diet.','deny a claim (= say it is not true ) Government officials denied claims that the country possessed chemical weapons.','dispute/reject a claim (= say it is not true ) The prime minister rejected claims of a disagreement within his party.','support a claim The court found no evidence to support her claim.','back up a claim (= support it ) They challenged him to back up his claims with evidence.','accept a claim Many scientists were reluctant to accept his claims.','challenge a claim (= say that you do not believe it is true ) Washington continued to challenge the claim that global warming is partly caused by carbon dioxide.','investigate a claim Detectives are investigating claims that the two officials took bribes.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('55322348-c3f1-50f1-ab96-1ab4cbcb0608','3696b85d-e5a4-5479-81e1-5785a349d2dc',5,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'somebody’s/something’s claim to fame','ادعا، بهانه؛ مطالبه؛ ادعای زمین','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['false His claims were later found to be false.','unfounded/unsubstantiated (= not based on truth or evidence ) These claims of discrimination are completely unfounded.','extravagant claims (= clearly not true ) Some manufacturers make extravagant claims for their products.','competing claims the competing claims of the political parties','conflicting claims (= saying that different things are true ) The reports contained conflicting claims of the number of people killed.','make a claim He made extravagant claims about the benefits of the diet.','deny a claim (= say it is not true ) Government officials denied claims that the country possessed chemical weapons.','dispute/reject a claim (= say it is not true ) The prime minister rejected claims of a disagreement within his party.','support a claim The court found no evidence to support her claim.','back up a claim (= support it ) They challenged him to back up his claims with evidence.','accept a claim Many scientists were reluctant to accept his claims.','challenge a claim (= say that you do not believe it is true ) Washington continued to challenge the claim that global warming is partly caused by carbon dioxide.','investigate a claim Detectives are investigating claims that the two officials took bribes.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('51b77b7c-aa05-54ed-a2be-27d990e0de8c','3696b85d-e5a4-5479-81e1-5785a349d2dc',6,'land','زمین','spoken & written','something such as a piece of land that contains valuable minerals',null,null,'چیزی مانند یک قطعه زمین که حاوی مواد معدنی ارزشمند است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['false His claims were later found to be false.','unfounded/unsubstantiated (= not based on truth or evidence ) These claims of discrimination are completely unfounded.','extravagant claims (= clearly not true ) Some manufacturers make extravagant claims for their products.','competing claims the competing claims of the political parties','conflicting claims (= saying that different things are true ) The reports contained conflicting claims of the number of people killed.','make a claim He made extravagant claims about the benefits of the diet.','deny a claim (= say it is not true ) Government officials denied claims that the country possessed chemical weapons.','dispute/reject a claim (= say it is not true ) The prime minister rejected claims of a disagreement within his party.','support a claim The court found no evidence to support her claim.','back up a claim (= support it ) They challenged him to back up his claims with evidence.','accept a claim Many scientists were reluctant to accept his claims.','challenge a claim (= say that you do not believe it is true ) Washington continued to challenge the claim that global warming is partly caused by carbon dioxide.','investigate a claim Detectives are investigating claims that the two officials took bribes.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('d85c13e2-5927-58b9-82b0-d787773a6e00','1e2970d2-3f3c-565a-9833-f3b4456fb7ab',1,'social group','گروه اجتماعی','spoken & written','one of the groups in a society that different types of people are divided into according to their jobs, income , education etc','[ countable ]','lower class , middle class , upper class , working class , → the chattering classes','طبقه (اجتماعی)؛ کلاس (درس)؛ رده، نوع','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['social class Is there a link between crime and social class?','the working/lower class At this time most of the working class was very poor.','the middle class A new middle class emerged after the war.','the upper class Members of the upper class didn’t have to work.','the ruling class (= the people in power ) For a long time, French was the language of the ruling class.','the professional class (= the people with professional jobs ) Doctors, lawyers, and teachers are all members of the professional class.','the landowning/landed class (= the people who own land ) This imposition of taxes angered the landed classes.','the educated class The educated classes shared certain values and experiences.','the privileged class (= people with advantages because of their wealth, social position etc ) Holidays abroad used to be only for the rich and privileged classes.','belong to a class Like you, I belong to the working class.','be a member of a class I suppose I’m a member of the middle class.','a class system/structure (= a social system that has classes ) He felt he was a victim of the class system.','a class division Nowadays, class divisions are related to economic status.','class differences (= differences that exist because of your class ) There are noticeable class differences in family size.','the class struggle/war (= disagreement or fighting between different classes ) the class struggle between workers and capitalists','class conflict This is the basis of class conflict in capitalist society.','class consciousness (= being aware of what class people belong to ) There is a high level of class consciousness among the workers.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a member of the landed class (= people who own land )","translation":"عضوی از طبقه زمین دار (= افرادی که صاحب زمین هستند)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663249.mp3"},{"sentence":"Defining the concept of class is not an easy task.","translation":"تعریف مفهوم کلاس کار ساده ای نیست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663258.mp3"},{"sentence":"The class system is slowly disappearing.","translation":"سیستم طبقاتی کم کم دارد از بین می رود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce6exa_00160.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('8b48c2fd-19a9-5a66-ab28-9f61d266f35c','1e2970d2-3f3c-565a-9833-f3b4456fb7ab',2,'students','دانش آموزان','spoken & written','a group of students who are taught together','[ countable ]',null,'گروهی از دانش آموزان که با هم آموزش می بینند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We’re in the same class for chemistry.","translation":"ما برای شیمی در یک کلاس هستیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce6exa_00161.mp3"},{"sentence":"Gary came top of the class in English.","translation":"گری در زبان انگلیسی در صدر کلاس قرار گرفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663263.mp3"},{"sentence":"My class are going to the science museum.","translation":"کلاس من به موزه علوم می رود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce6exa_00162.mp3"},{"sentence":"a class reunion","translation":"یک اتحاد مجدد کلاس","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663271.mp3"},{"sentence":"The class of ''69 spent almost as much time protesting as learning.","translation":"کلاس سال 69 تقریباً به اندازه یادگیری وقت خود را صرف اعتراض کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663275.mp3"},{"sentence":"The class was working on some maths problems.","translation":"کلاس روی چند مسئله ریاضی کار می کرد.","audio_url":null},{"sentence":"The class were working on some maths problems.","translation":"کلاس روی چند مسئله ریاضی کار می کرد.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,7),
('9f14544d-399e-58f6-b556-97ee12555327','1e2970d2-3f3c-565a-9833-f3b4456fb7ab',3,'teaching period','دوره تدریس','spoken & written','a period of time during which someone teaches a group of people, especially in a school','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'دوره زمانی که در طی آن شخصی به گروهی از افراد به خصوص در یک مدرسه آموزش می دهد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I missed Bible class last week.","translation":"هفته پیش کلاس کتاب مقدس را از دست دادم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663278.mp3"},{"sentence":"No talking in class!","translation":"صحبت کردن در کلاس ممنوع!","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001078995.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was injured in a science class.","translation":"او در کلاس علوم مجروح شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000318.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('051f4951-3c8a-58fb-a163-c3ec6d19d05f','1e2970d2-3f3c-565a-9833-f3b4456fb7ab',4,'studying','مطالعه کردن','spoken & written','a series of classes in a particular subject','[ countable ]',null,'مجموعه ای از کلاس ها در یک موضوع خاص','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a class in photography at night school","translation":"کلاس عکاسی در مدرسه شبانه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001079015.mp3"},{"sentence":"a dance class","translation":"یک کلاس رقص","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000319.mp3"},{"sentence":"Cindy’s taking a class on dealing with stress.","translation":"سیندی در کلاس مقابله با استرس شرکت می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663294.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('57986ab6-7896-5039-b633-6110714ea722','1e2970d2-3f3c-565a-9833-f3b4456fb7ab',5,'same type of something','همان نوع چیزی','spoken & written','a group of people, animals, or things that are considered together because they are similar in some way','[ countable ]',null,'گروهی از مردم، حیوانات یا چیزهایی که با هم در نظر گرفته می شوند زیرا به نوعی شبیه به هم هستند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Have you passed a test for this class of vehicle?","translation":"آیا آزمونی را برای این کلاس خودرو قبول کرده اید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663300.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('85e2daf1-b127-5891-b06a-2fc1d56cf9bf','1e2970d2-3f3c-565a-9833-f3b4456fb7ab',6,'train/aircraft etc','قطار / هواپیما و غیره','spoken & written','one of the different standards of seats , food etc available on a train, aircraft etc','[ countable usually singular ]',null,'یکی از استانداردهای مختلف صندلی، غذا و غیره موجود در قطار، هواپیما و غیره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We always travel first class.","translation":"ما همیشه درجه یک سفر می کنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663308.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('c731e0be-85dc-5b8f-9255-2d2a61e54e04','1e2970d2-3f3c-565a-9833-f3b4456fb7ab',7,'quality','کیفیت','spoken & written','a group into which people or things are divided according to their quality or abilities','[ countable ]',null,'گروهی که افراد یا اشیاء بر اساس کیفیت یا توانایی هایشان به آن تقسیم می شوند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The port now attracts a wealthier class of visitor.","translation":"این بندر اکنون طبقه ثروتمندتری از بازدیدکنندگان را به خود جذب می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663334.mp3"},{"sentence":"Its sheer versatility puts this computer in a different class.","translation":"تطبیق پذیری کامل آن، این کامپیوتر را در کلاسی متفاوت قرار می دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001079042.mp3"},{"sentence":"He’s not in the same class (= not as good ) as her at tennis.","translation":"او در همان کلاس (= نه به خوبی او) در تنیس نیست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001079046.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('ccb70e0a-8607-5a3b-bc4b-3cd84387e33b','1e2970d2-3f3c-565a-9833-f3b4456fb7ab',8,'style/skill','سبک/مهارت','informal','a high level of style or skill in something','[ uncountable ]','high-class , low-class','سطح بالایی از سبک یا مهارت در چیزی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The team showed real class in this afternoon’s match.","translation":"این تیم در بازی بعدازظهر امروز کلاس واقعی نشان داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001079078.mp3"},{"sentence":"A fountain will give your garden a touch of class .","translation":"یک فواره به باغ شما جلوه ای درجه یک می دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001663341.mp3"},{"sentence":"Laughton is a class act who’s proved his worth in the game.","translation":"لتون یک بازی کلاسی است که ارزش خود را در این بازی ثابت کرده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001079085.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('bd1a06fa-b4e2-57f0-8c5c-12b07501eb88','1e2970d2-3f3c-565a-9833-f3b4456fb7ab',9,'university degree','مدرک دانشگاهی','spoken & written','one of the three levels of a university degree','[ countable ]',null,'یکی از سه سطح مدرک دانشگاهی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a second class degree","translation":"مدرک درجه دو","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001079093.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('9bce684f-3ecb-524b-bede-a54fa087aee4','b6fca50e-ff83-50cb-82df-cdd395213bcf',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to consider people, things etc as belonging to a particular group, using an official system',null,null,'در نظر گرفتن افراد، اشیا و غیره به عنوان متعلق به یک گروه خاص، با استفاده از یک سیستم رسمی',array['classify']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Heroin and cocaine are classed as hard drugs.","translation":"هروئین و کوکائین جزو مواد مخدر سخت طبقه بندی می شوند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000888353.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('fa3406ec-b21e-593f-9ab5-d2324913a4a9','8ed32680-efd1-5a80-9cf7-22c7428569e2',1,'not dirty','کثیف نیست','spoken & written','without any dirt , marks etc',null,null,'تمیز، پاکیزه؛ خالی (سابقه)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['clean clothes He had a shower and changed into clean clothes.','a clean shirt/sheet/towel etc Where are all my clean socks?','clean hands Make sure you have clean hands before you eat.','keep something clean You should always keep your kitchen clean.','wipe something clean (= use a cloth to clean a surface ) He started to wipe the blackboard clean.','sweep/scrub something clean (= use a brush to clean something ) She quickly swept the floor clean.','leave something clean Please leave the apartment clean when you go.','spotlessly/scrupulously clean (= very clean ) Hospitals must be kept scrupulously clean.','squeaky clean (= completely clean ) I like my hair to be squeaky clean.','nice and clean (= clean ) Their job is to keep the streets nice and clean.','clean and tidy especially British English: I insist my children keep their rooms clean and tidy.','neat and clean especially American English: Her kids were always neat and clean.','clean as a whistle (= very clean ) The place was clean as a whistle.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Are your hands clean?","translation":"آیا دستان شما تمیز هستند؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001941630.mp3"},{"sentence":"clean towels","translation":"حوله تمیز","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001941631.mp3"},{"sentence":"Make sure you keep the wound clean .","translation":"مطمئن شوید که زخم را تمیز نگه دارید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001941632.mp3"},{"sentence":"Wipe that sink clean when you’re done.","translation":"وقتی کارتان تمام شد آن سینک را پاک کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001941638.mp3"},{"sentence":"As usual, she left her room clean and tidy before going to school.","translation":"طبق معمول قبل از رفتن به مدرسه اتاقش را تمیز و مرتب ترک کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001941673.mp3"},{"sentence":"a spotlessly clean kitchen","translation":"یک آشپزخانه کاملا تمیز","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001941644.mp3"},{"sentence":"I want you to get those plates as clean as a whistle .","translation":"من از شما می خواهم که آن بشقاب ها را مانند یک سوت تمیز کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001941648.mp3"}]'::jsonb,7),
('e96f73ba-5c44-5495-80b0-020224a055cd','8ed32680-efd1-5a80-9cf7-22c7428569e2',2,'people/animals','مردم / حیوانات','spoken & written','having a clean appearance and habits',null,null,'داشتن ظاهر و عادات تمیز','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['clean clothes He had a shower and changed into clean clothes.','a clean shirt/sheet/towel etc Where are all my clean socks?','clean hands Make sure you have clean hands before you eat.','keep something clean You should always keep your kitchen clean.','wipe something clean (= use a cloth to clean a surface ) He started to wipe the blackboard clean.','sweep/scrub something clean (= use a brush to clean something ) She quickly swept the floor clean.','leave something clean Please leave the apartment clean when you go.','spotlessly/scrupulously clean (= very clean ) Hospitals must be kept scrupulously clean.','squeaky clean (= completely clean ) I like my hair to be squeaky clean.','nice and clean (= clean ) Their job is to keep the streets nice and clean.','clean and tidy especially British English: I insist my children keep their rooms clean and tidy.','neat and clean especially American English: Her kids were always neat and clean.','clean as a whistle (= very clean ) The place was clean as a whistle.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Cats are naturally clean.","translation":"گربه ها به طور طبیعی تمیز هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001941654.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
